---
id: RS-005
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: todo!() or unimplemented!() shipped
version: 1

severity: warning
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 1

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(macro_invocation macro: (identifier) @name) @target'

related: []
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

A `todo!()` / `unimplemented!()` macro panics the moment a caller reaches it —
shipping one is a runtime abort waiting to happen. Finish the implementation, or
return a real error and open a ticket for the gap.

If a stub is genuinely deliberate (e.g. a doc-only signature), suppress with the
reason: `// @anvil-ignore RS-005 -- doc-only stub`. Test code (`#[cfg(test)]`
modules and `tests/` / `benches/` / `examples/` targets) is excluded
automatically.
